codex
The cause is concrete: Lean 4.22 asks for `/proc/<its namespace PID>/exe`, but this managed sandbox exposes the executable only through `/proc/self/exe`; the raw trace shows `/proc/2/exe → ENOENT`. I added a narrowly scoped, auditable `readlink` fallback under `/tmp/audit-work` that changes only this executable-path lookup. With that environment workaround, `lean --version` reports the pinned commit, so I’m rerunning the unchanged trusted preflight now.
